					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Ok. So I was scouring the Foundation, because I had an idea similar to this, and I wanted to make sure it hasn't been done before. Would it be acceptable if I try to write a main page article on a japanese H game (more of a dating sim with less emphasis on the H part) that causes anyone, of any gender or age, to become attached to the customizable protagonist (probably an Imouto type, as they are easiest to draw non-romantic attachment to) to the point of being willing to protect thier digital &quot;sibling&quot; with their life, and lose interest in any thing other then spending time with it. The program will also be able to interact with the subject outside of the game (send and recieve texts, even if there is no way to imput a cell number, and potentially cause the subject to hallucenate the character in real life) No foundation references in the characters though. Any thoughts?</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
